    "summary": "Turn 18 reviewed the artifact that adds the commit-propagation observation, the last unreviewed result on the confirmed recovery finding.\n\nState on entry. Artifacts 6a3e98cc… and 8c65f177… are confirmed in scope (violated, reviewed, no_issue_found). Artifact 4eb98b347aba4ff5ac999f8b89cdf836, executed as 36887d5bfbc643efbd4ed40b1e1cb4d5, reported violated with the oracle correspondence unreviewed. Its retained stream shows all three canonical events plus the new one: recovery_resolution with adopted_committed false, accept_round_after_commit with accept_oks 0 to 1, recovery_outcome with vectors_match false, and commit_propagation_divergence with replica0 NONE, replica1 PUT, replica2 NONE and all_committed_match false.\n\nReview judgement (checker_correspondence, no_issue_found). The three properties encode the same obligation in resolution, two-record and cluster form, each read with the raw fields printed beside it. The Commit under test is produced by the real bcastCommit inside handleAcceptReply and delivered through the real wire form to the already-committed replica (whose handleCommit returns early because its status is already COMMITTED) and to a third replica that installs the command as a legal receiver; the third replica's absence during the earlier rounds is a harness schedule choice, not a protocol assumption. Identity is the instance throughout; the oracle compares each replica's committed command for that instance, which is the agreement question itself. Legal history is bounded and declared: the already-committed record is prepared, so the check fixes the recovery rounds and the propagation, and it treats a replica's COMMITTED record as the protocol's own evidence of a chosen value, which is how a status-COMMITTED PrepareReply is treated in the resolution under review. No wait, join or cleanup duty is implied because every handler is synchronous and the event is emitted after both deliveries.\n\nReservations are stated as limitations: the committed record is prepared rather than produced by a proposal round; the property compares records rather than applied state, so the state-machine consequence remains a separate observation; and the third replica's record says nothing about earlier rounds. If accepted, the consequence of the confirmed adoption defect is confirmed at cluster level: after the recovery's Commit broadcast, one instance carries two different committed commands (NOOP on the recovering and third replicas, PUT on the replica that had committed), so the broadcast does not repair the disagreement. No map object, requirement, premise or earlier observation was changed."
